---
import MainLayout from "../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
---

<MainLayout
  title="StayJustIn | West Covina News, City Hall Updates & Development"
  description="StayJustIn covers West Covina City Hall, Athens Services trash rates, development projects, public safety updates, budgets, business changes, events, and community issues explained simply."
  canonical="https://www.stayjustin.com/"
>
  <section class="news-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">West Covina in simple terms</span>
      <h1>What’s Happening in West Covina Right Now</h1>
      <p>
        Clear updates on City Hall, development, budgets, public safety, and local issues —
        explained without the noise.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <p class="article-principle">
    <span>“Speak up for those who cannot speak for themselves.”</span><br />
    <strong>— Proverbs 31:8</strong>
  </p>

  <section class="featured-section">
    <div class="container">
      <article class="featured-card">
        <span class="featured-badge">Featured Investigation</span>
        <h2>
          <a href="/city-hall/athens-services-west-covina-trash-contract-rate-increases-2048/">
            Athens Services West Covina: The Trash Contract, Rate Increases, and Why Residents Are Locked In Until 2048
          </a>
        </h2>
        <p>
          West Covina’s long-term Athens Services agreement affects trash rates,
          City leverage, state-mandated organic waste rules, enforcement policies,
          and future flexibility for residents and businesses.
        </p>
        <a class="read-more" href="/city-hall/athens-services-west-covina-trash-contract-rate-increases-2048/">
          Read the Athens breakdown →
        </a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header clean-header">
        <div>
          <h2 class="section-title">Latest City Hall Stories</h2>
          <p class="section-sub">The main issues residents should be watching.</p>
        </div>
        <a class="view-all" href="/city-hall/">View City Hall</a>
      </div>

      <div class="story-grid">
        <article class="story-card">
          <span class="story-tag">Trash Rates</span>
          <h3>
            <a href="/city-hall/athens-services-west-covina-trash-contract-rate-increases-2048/">
              Athens Services contract explained
            </a>
          </h3>
          <p>
            Why West Covina’s trash agreement still affects rates, leverage, and residents today.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="story-card">
          <span class="story-tag">Budget Watch</span>
          <h3>
            <a href="/city-hall/west-covina-may-19-budget-special-events-questions/">
              May 19 meeting raised budget and staffing questions
            </a>
          </h3>
          <p>
            Event funding, staffing shortages, public land negotiations, and long-term costs.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="story-card">
          <span class="story-tag">City Hall</span>
          <h3>
            <a href="/city-hall/what-residents-miss-city-council-meetings/">
              What residents often miss during City Council meetings
            </a>
          </h3>
          <p>
            Emergency resolutions, ENAs, AB 1234 reports, and council requests explained.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="story-card">
          <span class="story-tag">Fire Station 3</span>
          <h3>
            <a href="/city-hall/fire-station-3-emergency-repairs-continue/">
              Fire Station 3 emergency repairs continue
            </a>
          </h3>
          <p>
            Why emergency authority matters for bidding, costs, and accountability.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header clean-header">
        <div>
          <h2 class="section-title">Development Projects to Watch</h2>
